WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:01.920
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.430
- Kiting does feel like flying

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.860
because sometimes we
actually do leave the ground

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.880
and actually fly through the air.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.920
The feeling when you're
riding behind a snowkite

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.850
is unlike any other feeling in the world.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.210
Just total freedom,

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.730
it's a combination of
feeling like you're flying

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.710
or gliding across the
ground with no resistance,

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.613
no effort and just a ton
of wind in your face.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.293
My name is Tom Fredericks,
and I'm a snowkiter.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.750
Snowkiting is basically getting pulled

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.970
on the snow with a giant kite.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.570
To be able to snowkite,
you need a big 4-line kite,

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:45.223
a waist harness that you
hook into in your skis.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.870
Twelve years ago, I moved to Alaska

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:51.160
to establish the first
kiteboarding and snowkiting school.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.393
I fell in love with the
mountains and the open air.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.520
Thompson Pass is one of
the best snowkiting venues

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.410
in the United States, if not the world.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.130
Just because of the plentiful
snow, the wide open terrain

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.500
and the steep mountains.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.783
It makes it truly a world class venue.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.185
Alaska Kite Adventures puts on

00:01:15.185 --> 00:01:17.230
the Snowkite Festival every year.

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:21.200
We have about 30 to 45
snowkiters come out to compete.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.440
At the Snowkite Festival, we offer clinics,

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.310
races and competitions,

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.730
and also a community forum
for us to exchange ideas

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.003
and teach the public about snowkiting.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.610
I think snowkiting is so unique as a sport

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.790
because it's been overlooked
for so many years.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.880
It has a small group of
passionate followers.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.210
The snowkite community
for me is so important

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.430
because it is a legacy
that I helped start.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.880
And to go from seeing
like two or three people

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.530
when I first moved up here 12 years ago,

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.440
to about 200 people snowkiting in Alaska,

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.859
that's super important.

00:01:57.859 --> 00:01:59.942
(cheers)

